title: 'sp-api: write back `transaction_depth` after `execute_in_transaction`'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    `ApiExt::execute_in_transaction` in the generated client-side `RuntimeApiImpl` incremented
    `transaction_depth` but discarded the result of `checked_sub(1)`, so the counter never
    returned to zero. Every later plain runtime API call on the same instance then skipped its
    own transaction, and overlay changes of a call returning `ApiError` were kept instead of
    being rolled back.

    The decremented value is now written back. On an API instance that has already completed
    an `execute_in_transaction` scope, a failing plain runtime API call has its overlay changes
    discarded again, as documented for `ProvideRuntimeApi::runtime_api`.
crates:
- name: sp-api-proc-macro
  bump: patch
